cff-version: 1.2.0
title: PrimerJury
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Burak Aslancan
    family-names: Pak
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7793-2215"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Yerlifan/primerjury"
license: PolyForm-Noncommercial-1.0.0
abstract: >-
  qPCR primer design from amplicon sequencing data, built around independent
  verification. Identity is established without a taxonomy tree, by seed and
  full alignment across twelve reference databases, and a claim is only
  accepted when at least two independent databases agree. Primer specificity
  is then checked by four layers deliberately built on different mechanisms
  (in-sample in-silico PCR, local databases, MFEprimer, NCBI Primer-BLAST);
  when the layers disagree the pair is blocked rather than averaged.
keywords:
  - qPCR
  - primer design
  - amplicon sequencing
  - nanopore
  - microbiome
  - taxonomic identification
  - specificity validation
